cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Aurora NERVE: Learned Motion Prediction in Supersonic Flight"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Prabhakaran Saravanakumar"
    given-names: "Kumar"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Canada"
date-released: "2026-10-08"
license: CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/kumarprabhakaransaravanakumar-wq/aurora-nerve-showcase"
abstract: >-
  A research programme on trustworthy learned prediction for high-speed flight,
  proposed as a passive, shadow-mode suborbital spaceplane payload. It compares
  learned and conventional gyro forecasts at 0.125-1 s horizons with frozen,
  pre-recorded predictions, and a fail-closed runtime-assurance architecture
  for bounded model-based reinforcement learning.
keywords:
  - learned motion prediction
  - supersonic flight
  - runtime assurance
  - model-based reinforcement learning
  - world models
  - flight-test instrumentation
  - suborbital spaceplane
